92	### Credentials (`git-credentials.ts`)
93	
94	```typescript
95	function extractHost(url: string): string | null
96	function injectCredentials(url: string, credentials: Record<string, string>): string
97	function hasEmbeddedCredentials(url: string): boolean
98	function stripEmbeddedCredentials(input: string): string
99	```

100	
101	> **`stripEmbeddedCredentials` contract:** Accepts an arbitrary string — not just a URL. Pure HTTPS URLs are sanitised via the WHATWG URL object (clean userinfo removal). All other inputs (non-HTTPS URLs, git prose error messages such as `"fatal: repository 'https://token@host/...' not found"`, and unparseable values) fall through to a regex scrub that replaces any `https?://…@` pattern with `https://***@`. Use this function on `gitResult.stderr` before surfaces it in API responses or logs.
